34)* (2.00) Found by t/display-random.t (2.07): a position from the
mouse (TkTextPixelIndex: "@x,y", and the mark "current", which every
redisplay sets where the pointer is) beyond the end of a display line
whose last chunk ended with a multi-byte character was inside that
character: DLinePixelIndex answered the last byte of the chunk (its
numChars counts bytes).  A mark set there split the character's bytes
into two segments, which became NUL bytes; the line then lost
characters ("1.end" moved back) and "get" gave malformed UTF-8.  With
30 "\x{221e}" in a widget 8 characters wide, -wrap char, ".t mark set
m @500,5" was enough.  TkTextIndexOfX (2.03) already backed up to the
character's start for itself; the mouse path was not checked (the
